# Hermetica — .gitignore
#
# A denylist. New files are tracked by default and show up in `git status`;
# anything that must not ship needs a rule here.
#
# The guard against committing a secret is `detect-secrets` in
# .pre-commit-config.yaml and in CI, which reads file *contents*. This file only
# handles paths: credentials, real protocol data, and build noise.


# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Matches a file named .env at any depth, so env/.env and security/.env are both
# covered. security/.baseline.security is deliberately tracked: it is the record
# of what detect-secrets has already reviewed, not a secret.
.env
.env.*
*.env


# --- Real protocol data -----------------------------------------------------
# The pull writes here (DB_OUT, LOGS). Real titles, authors, DOIs and bodies —
# none of it leaves this machine.
db/
logs/
protocol_list.json

# Lock files carry pinned protocol bodies. The two dependency locks are not
# protocol data and are tracked.
*.lock
!flake.lock
!uv.lock

# Rendered protocols and scanned lab documents.
*.pdf
*.db


# --- Working notes ----------------------------------------------------------
# Context and evidence for the coder. Not part of the project.
CLAUDE.md
docs/
protocol-vc-context.md


# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
build/
dist/


# --- Nix --------------------------------------------------------------------
result
result-*


# --- OS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
